@* iOS-style toggle switch. Use @bind-Value for two-way binding. *@

@* aria-checked is spelled out rather than bound to the bool: Blazor renders false by dropping the
   attribute, and a switch with no aria-checked reads as an ordinary button. The comment lives up
   here because a Razor comment inside a component's tag is sent to the browser as an attribute
   name, which throws and takes the whole circuit down with it. *@
<HomeButton Variant="bare"
            Size="none"
            role="switch"
            aria-checked="@(this.Value ? "true" : "false")"
            Class="@this.GetClasses()"
            Disabled="this.Disabled"
            OnClick="this.ToggleAsync">
    <span class="@this.GetThumbClasses()"></span>
</HomeButton>
